WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.500
The Shuttle board
A short tour of the Desk and Chronicle
Screenshots of the real board, over a fictional example

2
00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:08.500
The Desk groups tasks by what needs attention.

3
00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:12.200
Here, the tasks belong to a fictional workshop.

4
00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:17.700
Drafts: tasks written down, but not started.

5
00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:22.930
In flight: an agent, called a worker, is running on each of these.

6
00:00:23.030 --> 00:00:27.570
The card names the task and the result it should reach.

7
00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:32.200
Aloft marks a running worker. Click it to open that worker’s conversation.

8
00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:37.430
Awaiting review: a worker finished and recorded an outcome.

9
00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:42.070
This outcome says what still needs confirming before the workshop.

10
00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:46.700
Temper accepts the result. Discard sets it aside.

11
00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:51.000
Chronicle, the second tab, lays each task along the calendar.

12
00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:54.700
Marks show the days its workers were busy, through today.

13
00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:59.500
Set up Shuttle
Start with one machine and one small task
